<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-CANADA BEAT SWEDEN 3-1 TO LEVEL SERIES.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-CANADA BEAT SWEDEN 3-1 TO LEVEL SERIES.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the second game in the</p>
<p>best-of-three ice hockey world championship pool A final on</p>
<p>Tuesday:</p>
<p>Sweden 1 Canada 3 (0-0 1-2 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Per Eklund (30:56)</p>
<p>Canada - Geoff Sanderson (29:11), Anson Carter (38:09), Mark</p>
<p>Recchi (47:32)</p>
<p>Penalties: Sweden 8 minutes, Canada 20 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,316.</p>
<p>Final tied at 1-1. Third game to be played on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
